        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-02T18:13:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking at the [markarth configuration](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/HEAD:src/platform/ec/zephyr/program/skyrim/markarth/project.overlay;l\u003d196), I see the board has two f75303 devices installed.\n\nHowever, this driver assumes that there is only one device installed, but with the 3 temperature sensor types (local, remote_1, remote_2).\n\nThis driver needs to be refactored significantly to support multiple f75303 devices.\n\nFor a specific f75303 device, I recommend that you add devicetree property to the [yaml file](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/HEAD:src/platform/ec/zephyr/dts/bindings/temp/cros-ec,temp-sensor-f75303.yaml;l\u003d11) to specify the f75303 temperature type.\n\n```\nproperties:\n  temperture-type:\n    type: string\n    description:\n      Temperature \n    enum:\n      - F75303_LOCAL\n      - F75303_REMOTE_1\n      - F75303_REMOTE_2\n```\n\nThe devicetree entries would then look like:\n\n```\n\tsoc_f75303_local: soc-f75303-local@48 {\n\t\tcompatible \u003d \"cros-ec,temp-sensor-f75303\";\n\t\treg \u003d \u003c0x48\u003e;\n\t\ttemperature-type \u003d \"F75303_LOCAL\";\n\t};\n\tsoc_f75303_remote_1: soc-f75303-remote-1@48 {\n\t\tcompatible \u003d \"cros-ec,temp-sensor-f75303\";\n\t\treg \u003d \u003c0x48\u003e;\n\t\ttemperature-type \u003d \"F75303_REMOTE_1\";\n\t};\n\tsoc_f75303_remote_2: soc-f75303-remote-2@48 {\n\t\tcompatible \u003d \"cros-ec,temp-sensor-f75303\";\n\t\treg \u003d \u003c0x48\u003e;\n\t\ttemperature-type \u003d \"F75303_REMOTE_2\";\n\t};\n\tamb_f75303_local: soc-f75303-local@4f {\n\t\tcompatible \u003d \"cros-ec,temp-sensor-f75303\";\n\t\treg \u003d \u003c0x4f\u003e;\n\t\ttemperature-type \u003d \"F75303_LOCAL\";\n\t};\n\tamb_f75303_remote_1: soc-f75303-remote-1@4f {\n\t\tcompatible \u003d \"cros-ec,temp-sensor-f75303\";\n\t\treg \u003d \u003c0x4f\u003e;\n\t\ttemperature-type \u003d \"F75303_REMOTE_1\";\n\t};\n\tamb_f75303_remote_2: soc-f75303@4f-remote-2 {\n\t\tcompatible \u003d \"cros-ec,temp-sensor-f75303\";\n\t\treg \u003d \u003c0x4f\u003e;\n\t\ttemperature-type \u003d \"F75303_REMOTE_2\";\n\t};\n```\n\nYou can then modify the the [temperature sensor shim](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/HEAD:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/temp_sensors.c;l\u003d219), to use a different read routine based on the `temperature-type`\n\n```\n#define TEMP_SENSOR_F7503_READ(named_id) \\\n    COND_CODE_1(DT_PROP(node_id, temperature_type) \u003d\u003d F75303_LOCAL), \\\n                (\u0026f75303_get_local_temp), ())  \\\n    COND_CODE_1(DT_PROP(node_id, temperature_type) \u003d\u003d F75303_REMOTE_1), \\\n                (\u0026f75303_get_remote_temp_1), ())  \\\n    COND_CODE_1(DT_PROP(node_id, temperature_type) \u003d\u003d F75303_REMOTE_2), \\\n                (\u0026f75303_get_remote_temp_3), ())  \\\n\n#define GET_ZEPHYR_TEMP_SENSOR_F75303(named_id)                  \\\n\t(\u0026(const struct zephyr_temp_sensor){                     \\\n\t\t.read \u003d TEMP_SENSOR_F7503_READ(named_id),        \\\n\t\t.thermistor \u003d NULL,                              \\\n\t\t.update_temperature \u003d f75303_update_temperature, \\\n\t\tFILL_POWER_GOOD(named_id) })\n\n```\n\nHowever, does the platform really need 6 temperature sensors (3 per f75303 device)?\n\nIf only one sensor is needed, then you can reuse the `.idx` field to store the f75303 type.\n\n```\n#define TEMP_F75303(named_id, sensor_id)                                \\\n\t[TEMP_SENSOR_ID(named_id)] \u003d {                                  \\\n\t\t.name \u003d DT_NODE_FULL_NAME(sensor_id),                   \\\n\t\t.idx \u003d DT_PROP(node_id, temperature_type),              \\\n\t\t.type \u003d TEMP_SENSOR_TYPE_BOARD,                         \\\n\t\t.zephyr_info \u003d GET_ZEPHYR_TEMP_SENSOR_F75303(named_id), \\\n\t}\n```\n\nYou still need to create separate read routines for local, remote_1, remote_2 to work correctly with the temperature sensor shim.",
